# {{ .prefix }}-executing-plans

<!-- awf:section positioning -->
The inline implementation chain iterates plan phases. Inline is selected per phase, so a mixed plan can hand subagent-driven phases to its companion.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section when-to-invoke -->
## When to invoke

Invoke for an accepted plan with an `inline` phase. Read every phase's declared execution mode; do not infer one mode for the whole plan.
<!-- awf:end -->

## Procedure

<!-- awf:section procedure-resolve-plan -->
1. Resolve the mutable plan and read its complete phase structure. A fresh owner assigned one phase or task may run `awf read plan <plan> <P[.T]>` for its executable closure, including the generated task scope notice, phase-owned Advances and Completes outcomes, Notes, and Phase close; all are phase-owner context only; projection changes neither phase ownership nor checkpoint boundaries and never gives a task helper commit, review, checkpoint, handoff, or outcome authority. Before mutation, validate the one immutable effort slug and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md` path, confirm either legacy `Effort: <slug>` or canonical `effort: <slug>` identity (the legacy form is deprecated and remains only until active efforts finish), and preserve one user-managed writer. Repository sources and current-state documentation outrank checkpoint prose, and standalone memory is forbidden.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section procedure-raise-concerns -->
2. You, the parent executing this plan, raise missing phase context, ownership, paths, checks, or closing subject with the user before editing.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section procedure-per-task -->
3. **Iterate phases, not tasks.** Per `{{ .layout.maintainableCodeDesign }}`, you preserve the plan's settled structural choices, including a bounded enabling refactor; reassess if grounded source contradicts them, stop rather than bolt correctness onto the wrong abstraction, and do not drift from the plan. You run `awf context <the phase's exact paths>` before editing.
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->
For an `inline` phase, the parent owns every ordered task, integration, staged check, gate, phase-closing commit, report-only phase review, focused settlement commits, and checkpoint. A batch may dispatch explicitly partitioned sequential commit-disabled helpers only; each is the `implementer` agent in its commit-disabled mode, whose rendered contract governs its path confinement, green obligation, escalation, and return shape. Each brief carries the effort slug and exact owned memory path as read-only context, and helpers never edit shared memory: {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value. Full tier definitions: the agent guide's workflow section.{{ else }}choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable. Full tier definitions: the agent guide's workflow section.{{ end }} You inventory each return, reject out-of-subset writes, retain shared-file ownership, run the deterministic post-check, and never delegate the phase commit. Stage the complete transaction; the phase-closing commit requires `awf check staged` and {{ with .vars.gateCmd }}`{{ . }}`{{ else }}the project's gate{{ end }} to pass - a wired pre-commit hook enforces both at commit time, and a manual run first is needed only in a clone without wired hooks (checkable with `git config core.hooksPath`; when in doubt, run both manually). Review settles before checkpointing.

<!-- awf:include checkpoint-routine -->

If an implementer stops dirty, first inventory `git status --short`, diff, completed and remaining work, and failed checks. Choose exactly one: complete inline; restore the known green baseline and restart the complete revised phase; or stop for required user input. An explicit ownership transfer includes the complete revised phase, inventory, completed and remaining work, and recovery verification. Never issue a blind successor instruction for one task or dispatch over a dirty checkout.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section tdd-opt-in -->
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section gate-tier-detail -->
{{ with .data.e2eSuitePaths }}Use the fuller gate when a phase touches a declared end-to-end surface: {{ range . }}`{{ .path }}` {{ end }}.{{ end }}
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section procedure-adr-final-commit -->
4. Apply non-final batches of the ADR's declared State changes operations (V2) atomically with their matching claims and lifecycle event in the owning phase. The final batch and the Implemented flip are owned by the terminal-review flow and land only after the applicable terminal review settles.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section procedure-non-adr-final-commit -->
5. Freeze a plan only in its declared final transaction after review settlement.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section terminal-step -->
6. After all settled phases, invoke `{{ .prefix }}-reviewing-impl`.
<!-- awf:end -->

## Notes
<!-- awf:section project-invariants -->
- Expected output is non-negotiable. Never weaken assertions or adjust a golden merely to pass.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section notes-gate -->
- Gates are mandatory; fix the root cause.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section notes-auto-commit -->
- Auto-commit the phase only when green.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section notes-one-concern -->
- One coherent phase concern per closing commit.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section notes-docs-travel -->
- Docs travel with behavior.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section red-flags -->
## Red flags

Do not turn ordered tasks into transaction boundaries, let helpers commit, or checkpoint before report-only review settlement.
<!-- awf:end -->
